        "response": "Based on the clinical trial protocol for TJ301 (Olamkicept), here are the specific hepatic-related exclusion criteria in detail:\n\n**Exclusion Criterion #11 \u2014 Known Clinically Relevant Chronic Liver Disease:**\n\nThis criterion covers **two scenarios**:\n\n**A) In the absence of a diagnosis of Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC)**, a subject is excluded if they have:\n- Serum transaminases **>2.5 \u00d7 ULN**, OR\n- Alkaline phosphatase **>2.5 \u00d7 ULN**, OR\n- Abnormalities in synthetic liver function tests judged by the investigator to be **clinically significant**\n\n**B) With a diagnosis of Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC)**, a subject is excluded if they have:\n- Serum transaminases **>3 \u00d7 ULN**, OR\n- Alkaline phosphatase **>3 \u00d7 ULN**, OR\n- Abnormalities in synthetic liver function tests including **total bilirubin >1.5 \u00d7 ULN**, judged by the investigator to be **clinically significant**\n\nAdditionally, **Exclusion Criterion #16** covers a related infectious hepatic condition:\n- Known concurrent **acute or chronic viral Hepatitis B or C infection** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p.11 & p.35)",
